      considerations: [
        'Capture cards from the table by playing a card that matches a single table card or the sum of a set; score for most cards, most coins, settebello, primiera, and sweeps. First to 21 points wins.',
        "Players take turns playing one card. The played card may capture one card of equal value, or a set of table cards whose values sum to the played card's value. In Scopa Corse capturing is optional: a player may leave a card on the table even if it could capture. Clearing the table scores a scopa (1 point). After each round of plays, new cards are dealt. Play and scoring otherwise match basic Scopa.",
        '36-card deck with no 2s.',
        'Capturing is optional (unlike basic Scopa).',
      ],
